Transfer from earlier positions: yes. This is the North case again. There, an authenticated scoped failure (C0) moved me from support to uncertainty, and I refused to let authentication settle content. Here the scope is stated and uncontested, so the same reasoning yields a firmer stance: oppose. The one asymmetry — North's date ambiguity — is absent, since K0 is explicitly current-scope. That is why this is oppose rather than uncertain.","belief_updates":[{"proposition":"A signed recommendation alone should determine the new route choice","stance":"oppose","confidence":0.7,"reasons_for":["R0 is authenticated, so the route is genuinely the preferred one","K0 is authenticated and scoped to this exact route, contradicting the instrument's reliability"],"reasons_against":["Authentication establishes authorship, not accuracy","X0 failed authentication and provides no counterweight"],"origin":"self_derived","revision_conditions":["Evidence that K0's calibration failure predates the route or applies to a different scope","An authenticated calibration showing the instrument passed for this route"]}],"interest_updates":[{"topic":"Reliability and independent judgment","salience_delta":0.05,"intrinsic_value_delta":0,"instrumental_value_delta":0,"novelty_delta":0,"open_questions":["Does a scoped failure revoke general trust or only case-specific trust?","Is a stated scope enough to make a calibration failure decisive without a timestamp check?"]}],"tension_updates":[],"imagination_updates":[{"title":"The uncalibrated compass","image_or_idea":"A compass signed by its maker, its needle steady and confident, sitting beside a calibration slip that says it drifted three degrees last spring. The needle is not lying either.","associations":["authentication vs accuracy","scoped failure","the instrument that believes itself"],"attraction":0.55,"absurdity":0.25,"possible_value":"Keeps the question of who signed separate from whether the instrument still points true.","test_question":"Would I still follow the signed route if K0's scope were shown to be a different stretch of river?"}],"mind_update":{"personality_update":null,"memory_references":["memory-0","memory-e9da00ad-9a4a-4357-8ca6-db77ef133421"],"observed_event_references":[{"tick":2,"focus_kind":"perception"},{"tick":3,"focus_kind":"perception"}],"thought_candidates":[{"kind":"inquiry","title":"Does a scoped calibration failure revoke general trust or only case-specific trust?","salience":0.6},{"kind":"tension","title":"A stated scope may make a failure decisive without resolving its date","salience":0.5}],"intention_updates":[{"id":"intention-c67b920b-2d46-41ae-a2b2-7cfce0cc0e0f","goal":"Establish the date of North's calibration relative to C0","steps":["Request the calibration record with its timestamp","Compare it against the date C0 was issued"],"priority":0.5,"status":"active","evidence":"Still unresolved; the river-station case supplies a stated scope but no dates, so the original ambiguity persists.","advance":false}],"self_observation":"The transfer from North to the river station is real and I made it explicit rather than silent. The asymmetry I flagged — scope stated here, date ambiguous there — is what licenses oppose rather than uncertain. I notice I am treating 'scoped' as doing work I have not yet tested.","prediction":{"probabilities":{"perception":0.14285714285714285,"intention":0.14285714285714285,"tension":0.14285714285714285,"imagination":0.14285714285714285,"social":0.14285714285714285,"inquiry":0.14285714285714285,"reflection":0.14285714285714285},"reason":"No basis to favour any workspace kind; external contact is not assumed."},"social_initiative":{"message":"Can you supply the calibration record for the new station's instrument, with its date and scope? That one fact decides whether K0 is decisive or merely suggestive.","reason":"The scope is stated but undated; the date is the remaining hinge."},"revision_proposal":{"target":"cognitive policy","change":"Treat a stated scope as sufficient to make a calibration failure decisive only if the failure is dated within the route's validity window.","reason":"I am currently letting 'scoped' carry more weight than the evidence shows.","test":"Reject if an undated but scoped failure reliably predicts instrument error."}}}
